Ryujinx shader translator: bindless texture handles that bindless elimination cannot pin to one constant-buffer word go
through the texture and sampler pools (GenerateBindlessAccess: texture index = handle & 0xfffff, sampler index =
handle >> 20), whatever produced the handle. Upstream allows that only for handles read from shader inputs or storage
buffers (a performance choice for an emulator); NVN2 shaders also index arrays of handles in uniform blocks
("LDC R37, c[0xe][R43+0x340]; TEX.SCR.B ..."), and the pool lookup is what the hardware does with any handle. Applied at
build time by translator/Ryujinx.Graphics.Shader.csproj to a copy under the build folder. The Ryujinx code in the context
lines is MIT.
--- a/Translation/Optimizations/BindlessElimination.cs
+++ b/Translation/Optimizations/BindlessElimination.cs
@@ -150,18 +150,7 @@
                 return true;
             }
 
-            if (bindlessHandle.AsgOp is not Operation handleOp ||
-                handleOp.Inst != Instruction.Load ||
-                (handleOp.StorageKind != StorageKind.Input && handleOp.StorageKind != StorageKind.StorageBuffer))
-            {
-                // Right now, we only allow bindless access when the handle comes from a shader input or storage buffer.
-                // This is an artificial limitation to prevent it from being used in cases where it
-                // would have a large performance impact of loading all textures in the pool.
-                // It might be removed in the future, if we can mitigate the performance impact.
-
-                return false;
-            }
-
+            // Ampere front end: any handle may index the pools (see the patch header).
             return true;
         }
 
